MRI (Magnetic Resonance Imaging) systems are advanced medical imaging devices that utilise strong magnetic fields, radiofrequency pulses and sophisticated software algorithms to generate high‑resolution, multi‑planar images of the body’s internal structures. These non‑invasive systems are indispensable for diagnosing neurological disorders, musculoskeletal injuries, cardiovascular diseases and oncological conditions. Core components include superconducting magnets, gradient coils, RF coils and powerful image‑reconstruction engines that together enable precise tissue characterization.
