What is MRI Systems?
MRI systems represent a class of diagnostic equipment that leverages nuclear magnetic resonance principles to produce detailed anatomical and functional images without ionising radiation. The technology relies on a strong static magnetic field (typically 0.5 T to 7 T), rapidly switched gradient fields for spatial encoding, and radiofrequency pulses to excite hydrogen nuclei. Modern scanners incorporate AI‑driven reconstruction, motion‑correction algorithms and advanced coil designs that collectively reduce scan time, improve image quality and enhance patient comfort.
